--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9c94e8900bdbef942ad19f626cdac685, type: 3}
  m_Name: Horizontal_Scene1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  sceneHeader: Scene 1
  sceneSubHeader: Messaging on the Membrane
  NarrationBeats:
  - narrationText: "After you eat a meal,  your intestines release a hormone, GLP-1,
      into your bloodstream.\r"
    narrationTrack:
      Guid:
        Data1: 326555515
        Data2: 1236087443
        Data3: 828369805
        Data4: -206252294
      Path: event:/VO/scene_01_01
  - narrationText: "This peptide hormone streams through your body, eventually reaching
      the Islets of Langerhans in your pancreas, where your pancreatic beta cells
      live\r\r"
    narrationTrack:
      Guid:
        Data1: -827224350
        Data2: 1290681316
        Data3: 1498527625
        Data4: 745873825
      Path: event:/VO/scene_01_02
  - narrationText: "Receptor proteins known as GLP1-R dot the membrane of the beta
      cell, idly swaying back and forth, ready to receive a hormone signal.\r\r"
    narrationTrack:
      Guid:
        Data1: -32655517
        Data2: 1127579538
        Data3: -255988326
        Data4: 898133604
      Path: event:/VO/scene_01_03
  - narrationText: "As the flood of GLP-1 swells near the beta cell surface, some
      of the hormone proteins stray close enough to the receptors to bind to the
      receptor\u2019s binding pockets.\r\r\r"
    narrationTrack:
      Guid:
        Data1: 2134581677
        Data2: 1139548894
        Data3: -69747547
        Data4: 2092874070
      Path: event:/VO/scene_01_04
  - narrationText: "This binding moment changes the receptor\u2019s shape, allowing
      it to interact with signaling proteins inside the cell. \r\r\r\r"
    narrationTrack:
      Guid:
        Data1: 631176908
        Data2: 1079216640
        Data3: 1145474458
        Data4: -527583183
      Path: event:/VO/scene_01_05
  - narrationText: "One of these signaling proteins, the G protein complex, becomes
      activated when interacting with the receptor here.\r\r\r\r"
    narrationTrack:
      Guid:
        Data1: 1792358708
        Data2: 1200576198
        Data3: -622862440
        Data4: -2085993692
      Path: event:/VO/scene_01_06
  - narrationText: "After activating, each G protein complex then splits into two.
      \r\r\r\r\r"
    narrationTrack:
      Guid:
        Data1: -758370899
        Data2: 1166018978
        Data3: -288975485
        Data4: 520725131
      Path: event:/VO/scene_01_07
  - narrationText: "One of the two halves, called G alpha, binds to another protein
      rooted on the membrane, AC.\r \r\r\r\r\r"
    narrationTrack:
      Guid:
        Data1: -547006053
        Data2: 1198535529
        Data3: -661307741
        Data4: 222133151
      Path: event:/VO/scene_01_08
  - narrationText: "While the G alpha and AC are bound together, they convert nearby
      energy molecules (ATP) into cAMP signaling molecules that travel deeper in
      the cell.\r\r \r\r\r\r\r"
    narrationTrack:
      Guid:
        Data1: 1422013404
        Data2: 1109065407
        Data3: 1778237318
        Data4: 1163785049
      Path: event:/VO/scene_01_09
  - narrationText: "These cAMP molecules simultaneously trigger both the release
      of stored insulin and the production of new insulin within the pancreatic beta
      cell.\r.\r\r \r\r\r\r\r"
    narrationTrack:
      Guid:
        Data1: 309815811
        Data2: 1082383009
        Data3: 907677856
        Data4: 47234537
      Path: event:/VO/scene_01_10
